    Record a change log and draw it as the timeline's rows

    Every real edit becomes one entry in state.json: what kind, OrcaSlicer's
    raw name, who made it, when, and which conversation item it follows. The
    Agent page merges consecutive identical entries into one row, as the Figma
    frame "print-timeline-panel-full · no revert" draws them, and a finished
    reply the Agent changed nothing after says "Answered · nothing changed".

    Detection reads state OrcaSlicer already keeps. Model edits are undo steps
    under OrcaSlicer's own snapshot_modifies_project rule, so selection, "!"
    steps such as plate switching, and slicing never count, and any feature
    that records an undo step is covered. Undo and redo are moves of the
    active position. Settings are changes between preset_deltas_of readings;
    a changed preset name is one switch, and a delta folded into a saved
    preset is not a change. Edits are a feed of their own, separate from
    WorkspaceChanged, so recording one never advances the revision; the tool
    coordinator's AgentEdit scope attributes edits to the Agent.

    OrcaSlicer footprint, two lines in Plater.cpp: set_plater_dirty notifies
    ProjectStateChangeReason::Modified when the project is marked dirty
    (custom G-code, plate settings, filament mapping, brim ears), and the
    fork's own take_snapshot notification carries UndoStep instead of None,
    which the hub dropped unless undo availability changed. Both flags are
    fork-owned and map to no workspace reason.

    The row's title-to-metadata gap is the new token
    component.threadRow.lineGap, emitted as --thread-row-line-gap.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

